  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Costumed marching bands of the Philadelphia Mummers Parade held every New Year's Day, organised as clubs rooted in the South Philadelphia neighbourhoods around Two Street and judged in a String Band Division. Parade rules bar brass instruments, so dozens of banjos and saxophones with accordions, violins, string basses, glockenspiels and drums play arranged popular songs and marches while the members strut in elaborate costumes; the Ferko String Band's 'Alabama Jubilee' became a national hit in 1955.",
